# Billing financial-integrity gate

- Do not add a new billing feature or financial path while this freeze is active.
- Allowed work: defect fixes, invariant tests, reconciliation, accessibility, and workflow simplification that adds no financial path.
- Preserve immutable invoice, payment, refund, reversal, stock-movement, and correction records.
- Keep one authoritative quick-billing issuance path and one active financial issue per visit.
- Every supply charge must link to inventory movements and preserve original batch, cost, and sale snapshots.
- Returned corrections restore the original batch; consumed corrections become wastage; neither may leave sale or COGS recognized.
- Payment-basis reports must be driven by immutable transaction dates and final settlement.
- Before completion, run the matrix in `docs/billing-accounting-invariant-matrix.md`, full server/client tests, client build, and one Bugbot review.
- Any new P1/P2 billing-integrity finding, lifecycle failure, or reconciliation exception fails the gate.
- Remove or relax this freeze only on explicit owner direction after the invariant and reconciliation suites remain green.
